From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:44:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: opp: adreno: add a bandwidth range per OPP

Qualcomm's GPU drivers let the DDR vote of a GPU OPP float between a
lowest and a highest bandwidth, following the GPU's measured memory
traffic, rather than tying it to the GPU clock. Describe that range.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-qcom-adreno.yaml    | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-qcom-adreno.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-qcom-adreno.yaml
index 0bd7d6b69..4df458716 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-qcom-adreno.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/opp-v2-qcom-adreno.yaml
@@ -36,6 +36,16 @@ patternProperties:
 
       opp-supported-hw: true
 
+      qcom,opp-peak-kBps-range:
+        description: |
+          The lowest and highest DDR bandwidth, in kBps, the GPU may vote at
+          this OPP when it scales its bus vote with its measured memory
+          traffic. opp-peak-kBps stays the vote it starts from.
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+        items:
+          - description: Lowest bandwidth in kBps
+          - description: Highest bandwidth in kBps
+
       qcom,opp-acd-level:
         description: |
           A positive value representing the ACD (Adaptive Clock Distribution,
-- 
